      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "स्वान् गुणान् see com.; as it stands, however, it is entirely objection-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "able. Mr. Telang thinks the construction of the stanza to be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "similar to that of Sis'. I. 51, which is according to the Sûtra",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "समुच्चयेऽन्यतरस्याम्. In such constructions all the verbs must be in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the Imperative mood. Here मावमंस्थाः must be considered as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "equivalent in sense to the Imperative mood. लक्षणम्—Mr. Telang",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "adopts the reading चेष्टितम्. But then what does एतद् refere to ?",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "Certainly to the actions indicated by छिन्धि &c.; so this amounts",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "to एतत् चेष्टितं सतां चेष्टितम्. लक्षणं is therefore better. Such acts are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "the the sign of &c.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 78. पुण्यपीयूष०—full of nectarious holiness or holy",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "thoughts &c. पर्वतीकृत्य—magnifying to the size of a mountain,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "making much of. कियन्तः—some, few, rare. Mr. Telang compares",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "with this the use of कश्चित् in Bhag. VII. 3. एतेन वाचा कर्मणा च सर्वे-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "षामुपकावरन्त इत्यर्थः । Rámarshi.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 79. हेमगिरि the mountain of gold, मेरु. रजताद्रि—Kailâsa,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "being white (on account of being covered with snow), is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "considered to be a mountain of silver. This cannot be Himà-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "laya as some take it. Cf. Meg. I. 58. यत्र &c.—The trees on",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "other mountains are the same that they are; they are not chang-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "ed into sandal trees as they would be if they grew on the Malaya",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "mountain. Malaya, a mountain in the south of India, famed for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "its sandal trees. मन्यामहे—we honour. Cf. अहमेव मतो महीपतेः Rag.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "VIII. 8. and Mallinàtha's com. thereon. The fig. is विरोधाभास.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 80. रत्नैर्महार्हैः—with the 13 valuable jewels (churned out",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "of the ocean before obtaining the 14th—nectar). भीमविषेण &c.—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "did not take affright at the appearance of the dreadful poison.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "निश्चितार्थात्—The abl. by the Vârt जुगुप्सा &c. see com. See A. G. §",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "76. Cf. प्रारब्धमुत्तमजना न परित्यजन्ति । The fourteen jewels are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "mentioned in the following verse—लक्ष्मीः कौस्तुभपारिजातकसुरा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "धन्वन्तरिश्चन्द्रमा गावः कामदुघाः सुरेश्वरगजो रम्भादिदेवाङ्गनाः । अश्वः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "सप्तमुखो विषं हरिधनुः शंखोमृतं चाम्बुधे रत्नानीह चतुर्दश प्रतिदिनं कुर्वन्तु वो",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "मङ्गलम् ॥ For the story, see Râmá. Bal. K. 45. Bhág. P. VII.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "9--8. Ni'. S'a, 27. The fig. here is अर्थान्तरन्यास.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
